Subject: [PATCH] handoff: record the path past one-slot answers before it is
 lost to context

A design thread reasoned through in conversation and nowhere in the repo.
Written down as design, marked unmeasured, so the next session inherits the
argument rather than re-deriving it.

The blocker for the stated goal is the answer interface, not the mind: answers
are slot indices and G_answer_is_slot is the separation proof, so composite
questions kill the proof the moment they are attempted. 289 answers with a
derivation - a verb from a small closed set plus a slot set - built from the
tape so labels stay free, and EXECUTED rather than generated, which makes
G_answer_is_derivation strictly stronger than what it replaces. 288 is already
the two-verb case.

Thought is defined as a write with provenance: an intermediate result either
lives in activations, unauditable, or becomes a derived slot marked with the
premises and the verb. The second keeps the invariant, extends 279 with
DERIVE, and makes conclusions revocable by the leak test that already exists.

One correction to something stated too absolutely earlier in the same thread.
No new VERB will emerge from data - capability is installed. But new CONTENT
can, because a discrete space has search where a continuous one has
interpolation; that is exactly why GPT exceeds its dataset and a tape cannot,
and it is the same property as auditability.

And the trap in generate-and-filter, named before anyone builds it: a filter
that accepts what agrees with the tape computes the tape's deductive closure
and saturates. Selection has to come from outside the population, and the free
outside is incoming text - a derived slot as a prediction with provenance,
confirmed or refuted later, with the verb that produced it gaining or losing
support. With the collapse guard that follows from provenance: derivation
depth, only depth-0 slots admissible as evidence, and only confirmation by
text resets depth. A thought becomes knowledge by passing through the world,
never through itself.

